# VR StandardPlayer skeleton template.
#
# The joint lines are not here yet: open your VR reference skeleton scene
# (the one the old jointOrient table was baked from, VR_Skeleton_Example.ma),
# select its top joint (Root) and press "Capture Template" with this file
# chosen. Capture keeps the #place rules below.
#
# Rules for joints a CC4 / AccuRig source can't supply (from the old
# build_locators_from_accurig.mel). {S} expands to L and R.
#place Root origin
#place Hand_Twist_01_{S} at Hand_{S}
#place Foot_Twist_01_{S} at Foot_{S}
#place Hand_Offset_{S} mid Hand_{S} Finger_2_0_{S}
#place Shield_Offset_{S} mid LowerArm_{S} Hand_{S}
#place Finger_1_3_{S} extend Finger_1_1_{S} Finger_1_2_{S} 0.5
#place Finger_2_3_{S} extend Finger_2_1_{S} Finger_2_2_{S} 0.5
#place Finger_3_3_{S} extend Finger_3_1_{S} Finger_3_2_{S} 0.5
#place Finger_4_3_{S} extend Finger_4_1_{S} Finger_4_2_{S} 0.5
# The old locator script put Pelvis on CC_Base_Pelvis, while the matchers
# (and the old rename script) use CC_Base_Hip. Uncomment to keep the old spot:
##place Pelvis src CC_Base_Pelvis
